.Dd October 11, 2026
.Dt WATTLE-DEPS 1
.Os Wattle DEVEL
.
.Sh NAME
.Nm wattle-deps
.Nd manage the dependencies of a project
.
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm "wattle deps"
.Ar verb
.
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm "wattle deps"
copies dependencies into the project in the current directory.
The sources to copy are declared under
.Ql ":vendored"
in the project’s info file.
Nothing is installed under
.Ql "*prefix*" .
See
.Xr wattle-dependencies 7
for vendoring and remote libraries.
.Pp
A build made without the OS library does not include
.Cm deps .
Each verb reports this limitation and exits with status 1.
.Ic d
is a synonym for
.Cm deps .
.
.Sh VERBS
.Bl -tag -width Ds -compact
.It Xo
.Cm vendor
.Xc
Copies the sources declared in
.Ql ":vendored"
into the project.
Each declaration is a map containing
.Ql ":name"
and
.Ql ":url" .
The URL specifies a source as for
.Cm install
in
.Xr wattle-apps 1 .
.Pp
Optional keys select what to copy and where to place it.
.Ql ":ref"
selects a Git branch or tag.
.Ql ":prefix"
specifies the destination directory and defaults to the current
directory.
.Ql ":paths"
is a vector of source paths or pairs of source and destination
paths.
Without
.Ql ":paths" ,
the whole source is copied.
See
.Sx "VENDORING"
in
.Xr wattle-dependencies 7
for the declaration keys and an example.
.Pp
Existing files are replaced.
Paths cannot be absolute or contain
.Ql "\&.\&." .
Every declaration is checked before any source is fetched,
and names must be unique.
Vendoring records no source revision;
the copied files become part of the project.
.El
.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Copy the vendored sources that
.Ql "info\&.edn"
lists into the current directory:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ wattle deps vendor
.Ed
.
